        "heading": "How it was traditionally used",
        "body": "In the classical framework, shilajit was employed as a broad rejuvenative and as a supportive addition (anupana or yogavahi — a 'carrier' thought to enhance other substances) in many formulations. Texts associate it with supporting energy, the urinary and reproductive systems, and healthy metabolism, and it was often combined with herbs and taken with warm milk or other vehicles.\n\nIt is worth being honest here: these are traditional indications framed in Ayurvedic concepts of dosha, agni and dhatu — not modern disease diagnoses. Classical use tells us what practitioners observed and valued over centuries; it does not, by itself, establish clinical proof by today's standards."
