    "intro": "Bone health is one of the most under-discussed aspects of women's wellbeing in India. From the demands of pregnancy and breastfeeding to the sharp drop in oestrogen at menopause, a woman's skeleton faces stresses that men's simply do not. Small wonder that many women searching for natural support come across shilajit and wonder whether this famous Himalayan resin can help keep bones strong.\n\nAs an Ayurvedic doctor, I want to give you an honest answer. Shilajit has a genuine mineral-rich rationale worth understanding — but it is not a bone medicine, and the modern evidence in women specifically is still thin. Here is what the tradition says, what science can and cannot confirm, and how to actually build bone health that lasts.",
