    "intro": "Shilajit is a mineral-rich exudate that Ayurveda has used for centuries as a rasayana (rejuvenative). Most healthy adults tolerate purified (shodhit) Shilajit well. But because it carries iron, other trace minerals and bioactive compounds like fulvic acid, it can — in theory and occasionally in practice — nudge how certain medicines behave in your body.\n\nThis article is educational, not a prescription. If you take regular medication, are managing a chronic condition, or are pregnant or breastfeeding, treat the sections below as a checklist to discuss with a qualified physician before adding Shilajit.",
