        "body": "Shilajit isn't a single molecule — it's a complex, mineral-dense substance. Its iron content, trace minerals and fulvic/humic compounds are exactly what make it interesting, but they are also the parts most likely to bump into a medicine. Minerals can bind to some drugs in the gut and reduce their absorption; certain constituents may add to or oppose what a medicine is already doing.\n\nIt's worth being clear about the evidence: much of what we understand about mineral-drug interactions comes from studies on iron, calcium and similar minerals generally, not from large clinical trials on Shilajit specifically. So the guidance here is precautionary and reasonable, not a proven certainty for every person."
