        "heading": "Test 3: Temperature & Texture Behaviour",
        "body": "Authentic resin is famously responsive to temperature. In cold weather or the fridge it becomes hard and brittle; in warm hands or warm weather it softens and becomes stretchy and pliable, like a thick tar. Roll a small piece between warm fingers — it should gradually become malleable.\n\nA product that stays the same consistency regardless of temperature, or that is uniformly soft and paste-like straight from the fridge, may be mixed with oils or humectants. Again, useful as a clue, not a verdict."
