        "body": "Triphala — the classical blend of Amalaki, Bibhitaki and Haritaki — is one of the traditional media used in the Shodhana of Shilajit. The raw resin is typically dissolved and processed in a Triphala decoction (kwath), then filtered and concentrated. Classical logic holds that Triphala's properties help draw out impurities while complementing Shilajit's own qualities.\n\nCow's milk, cow's ghee, Bhringraj and Gomutra are also mentioned as Shodhana media in different classical references. Triphala remains popular because it is gentle, widely available, and its own reputed benefits align well with how Shilajit is traditionally used. It's worth noting that while this tradition is well documented, head-to-head modern clinical comparisons of different purification media are limited."
