        "heading": "What Shilajit actually is (and why lifters care)",
        "body": "Shilajit is a blackish-brown resin that seeps from Himalayan rock over centuries. Its most-studied components are fulvic acid, humic substances and a spread of trace minerals. In Ayurveda it's classified as a Rasayana and Yogavahi — a carrier that's traditionally believed to enhance the action of other nutrients and support strength (Bala) and vitality (Ojas).\n\nFor gym-goers, the appeal is simple: it isn't a stimulant. Unlike caffeine or pre-workout blends, Shilajit doesn't spike your heart rate or leave you jittery and crashing. The interest is in steadier energy, better recovery capacity and mineral support — a slow, foundational effect rather than an instant hit."
