        "heading": "Traditional Uses in Ayurveda",
        "body": "Ayurvedic texts describe Triphala as a gentle digestive and eliminatory support — it is most often used to encourage regularity and comfortable digestion. It has also been traditionally used in eye care (as a wash), oral care, and as a general tonic within rasayana therapy.\n\nIt is worth being clear: these are classical uses rooted in centuries of practice, not disease treatments. Triphala is best understood as a supportive daily formulation rather than a cure for any specific condition."
