    "readTime": "7 min read",
    "intro": "\"Shilajit or ashwagandha — which one should I take?\" is one of the most common questions I hear in clinic. Both are respected in Ayurveda, both have modern research interest, and both are marketed heavily online. But they are not interchangeable. They come from very different sources, act on different aspects of your physiology, and suit different goals.\n\nThis guide compares them fairly — classical use alongside what modern science can and cannot yet confirm — so you can make a calm, informed choice rather than a hype-driven one.",
