        "heading": "Food and hydration come first",
        "body": "The most reliable, non-habit-forming support is dietary. Warm, moist, well-cooked foods generally suit a Vata-driven pattern better than cold, dry, or raw ones. Adequate water through the day, cooked vegetables, soaked raisins or prunes, and healthy fats like ghee are traditionally favoured because they add moisture and gentle lubrication. Modern nutrition agrees on the basics: soluble and insoluble fibre, plus fluids, support healthy bowel movements for most people.\n\nSmall habits matter too. Eating at roughly the same times, not skipping meals, chewing well, and giving the body a calm, unhurried morning routine all help your natural rhythm. A warm drink on waking is a simple, widely used nudge for the bowels."
