    "intro": "We often think of health in terms of what we eat, how we sleep, or how strong we feel. Ayurveda adds another quiet but powerful measure: how well the body clears out what it no longer needs. These waste products are called the malas, and classical texts pay them close attention.\n\nThe idea is simple. Just as a household stays comfortable only when the rubbish is taken out regularly, the body functions best when its natural elimination channels are open and moving. This article walks through the three malas, why Ayurveda considers them so important, and gentle, everyday ways to support healthy elimination — while being honest about what modern science does and doesn't yet confirm.",
