        "heading": "Safety and quality considerations",
        "body": "Ayurveda repeatedly stresses that Shilajit must be properly purified (shodhit) before use, because raw resin can carry heavy metals and other contaminants. Sourcing and processing therefore matter enormously — an unpurified or adulterated product is a genuine safety risk, not a bargain. Look for products that are lab-tested and transparent about purification.\n\nVajikarana therapy in the classical sense was never a self-prescribed, one-size-fits-all affair; it was individualised. Pregnant and breastfeeding women, anyone on regular medication, and those with chronic illness should consult a qualified physician before using any tonic, including Shilajit. The safest, most Ayurvedic approach is to treat these substances as supportive additions to a healthy routine — not miracle fixes."
