        "q": "What is the difference between Nidana and Samprapti?",
        "a": "Nidana refers to the causes of a disease — diet, lifestyle, season, stress and habits. Samprapti refers to the pathogenesis, meaning the sequence of events by which those causes progress into a visible illness. One asks 'why', the other asks 'how it unfolded'."
