        "body": "Shilajit is classically described as heating (ushna) in nature, so people often ask whether summer is the wrong time for it. The traditional workaround is the carrier (anupana): pairing Shilajit with a cooling medium can help balance that warmth. In summer, cool or room-temperature milk is a commonly favoured carrier, and small quantities matter more than large ones.\n\nAt 3TATTAVA this is exactly why we offer options like RockResin Shodhit Shilajit resin, which you can dissolve in cool milk, and Shahjeet Shilajit honey sticks for convenience. A word of caution honoured by tradition: honey should not be mixed into hot liquids. Keep carriers cool or warm-not-hot, listen to your body, and remember that consistency and moderation serve you better than intensity — especially in a heating season."
