        "body": "The Himalayan and adjoining ranges are the classical home of good-quality Shilajit in Ayurveda, and high-altitude sources are traditionally prized. The Kashmir region sits firmly within this favourable belt, so the raw material can genuinely be of good origin.\n\nThat said, the same geological conditions exist across hundreds of kilometres. Ladakh, Gilgit, parts of the Karakoram and the central Himalaya all yield Shilajit. Fixating on one valley name overlooks a bigger point: raw exudate from any of these places is unfit for use until it has been correctly cleaned and processed. Origin is the starting line, not the finish."
