        "heading": "How to verify before you buy",
        "body": "Ask for a batch-specific certificate of analysis from an accredited third-party laboratory (NABL-accredited in India, or equivalent). It should report heavy metals within permissible limits and screen for microbial contamination. A brand confident in its quality will share this readily; vague reassurance is a red flag.\n\nBeyond lab reports, look for transparency on sourcing region, purification method and, ideally, a fulvic-acid or ash-content figure. Physical checks help too — genuine resin is typically thick and sticky, softens with warmth and firms when cool, and dissolves in warm water without leaving gritty sediment. But no home test replaces a laboratory report."
