    "intro": "In Ayurveda, a Rasayana is a category of rejuvenative practices and preparations meant to nourish the tissues, support vitality and help the body age gracefully. Two names dominate this conversation in Indian homes: Shilajit and Chyawanprash. Both are revered, both are ancient — but they are quite different in what they are and how you use them.\n\nIf you have been standing in a shop (or scrolling online) trying to decide between the two, this guide breaks down the honest differences. My aim here is not to crown a \"winner,\" but to help you match the right Rasayana to your goal, routine and constitution — and to be clear about where evidence is strong versus still emerging.",
