    "intro": "If you have been reading about natural ways to support energy and stamina, two names keep coming up: shilajit and cordyceps. They are often mentioned in the same breath, as if they were rivals for the same job. They are not.\n\nOne is a mineral-rich resin that seeps from Himalayan rocks. The other is a fungus that grows on caterpillar larvae in high-altitude meadows. They come from different kingdoms of nature, contain different active compounds, and are traditionally used for different reasons. Understanding that difference helps you choose honestly, rather than picking whichever the internet shouted loudest about.",
