    "intro": "Premenstrual syndrome (PMS) — the cluster of physical and emotional symptoms that show up in the days before a period — is one of the most common reasons women look for natural support. Fatigue, low mood, bloating, cravings and irritability can make that week genuinely hard. Shilajit, the mineral-rich resin used in Ayurveda for stamina and rejuvenation, comes up often in these conversations. So does it actually help with PMS?\n\nThe honest answer: there is a reasonable traditional and nutritional rationale, but very little PMS-specific clinical research. This guide walks through what Shilajit is, why people connect it to premenstrual symptoms, and where the evidence genuinely stops — so you can make an informed, unhurried decision alongside your doctor.",
