        "heading": "The honest evidence gap",
        "body": "To our knowledge there are no well-designed, PMS-specific clinical trials on Shilajit — nothing that tracks premenstrual symptom scores in women taking Shilajit versus a placebo across several cycles. So any claim that Shilajit 'relieves PMS' is currently unsupported by direct evidence.\n\nThat doesn't make Shilajit useless; it means we should describe it accurately. If it helps some women, it's most likely through general energy, mood and micronutrient support rather than a specific effect on the premenstrual mechanism. Set expectations accordingly and judge by how you actually feel over time."
