        "body": "For PMS, the best-supported steps are unglamorous but effective: consistent sleep, regular movement, managing stress, limiting excess caffeine, salt and alcohol in the premenstrual week, and correcting deficiencies like iron, vitamin D, magnesium and B-vitamins where a doctor identifies them. Tracking your cycle helps you see patterns and test whether anything is truly making a difference.\n\nIf you choose to explore Shilajit, treat it as one small part of this foundation rather than a standalone solution. Quality matters — look for purified (shodhit) resin with transparent testing, since raw Shilajit can carry heavy-metal and contamination risks."
