    "intro": "In Ayurveda, most of us are not a single dosha but a blend. The Vata-Pitta constitution (prakriti) is one of the most common dual types — a person shaped by the movement and creativity of Vata alongside the fire and focus of Pitta.\n\nThis combination brings real strengths: quick thinking, drive, and adaptability. But when either dosha tips out of balance, the same person can swing between anxious restlessness and hot-headed intensity. This guide explains how to recognise a Vata-Pitta nature and how classical wisdom suggests keeping it steady — while being clear about where modern evidence is still thin.",
