    "readTime": "6 min read",
    "intro": "When people talk about Ayurveda as an \"ancient science\", they are usually pointing — knowingly or not — to a small set of remarkable books written and refined over many centuries. These classical Ayurvedic texts are where the theory, diagnosis and treatment traditions were first organised in a systematic way.\n\nUnderstanding them helps you separate genuine tradition from marketing folklore. In this article we'll walk through the three most celebrated texts — often called the Brihat Trayi, or \"Great Triad\" — and what each contributes, along with an honest note on how they sit alongside modern evidence.",
