    "intro": "Every hard training session breaks something down — muscle fibres, glycogen stores, fluids, even mental focus. What you do afterwards decides how well you rebuild. Modern sports science calls this \"recovery nutrition.\" Ayurveda has spoken about the same idea for centuries, only in its own language: rebuilding the dhatus (body tissues), rekindling agni (digestive fire) and restoring ojas (vitality and resilience).\n\nIn this article we'll look at how classical Ayurvedic thinking maps onto post-exertion recovery for athletes — what to eat, why warmth and rest matter, and where Rasayanas like Shilajit traditionally fit in. We'll also be honest about where solid modern evidence exists and where it's still limited, so you can make sensible, informed choices.",
